  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">WATC</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Women&apos;s Affairs Technical Comittee - WATC -  submitted a proposal related to youth civic engagement. Based on research they conducted they found that young people often experience social exclusion, limited access to leadership opportunities, and a lack of safe spaces to participate in governance and advocacy. Their project aims to equip youth with leadership, advocacy, and governance skills to increase their participation in decision-making and community initiatives.
In addition to fostering youth-led dialogue and initiatives that promote social unity, conflict resolution, and active participation in local governance.
The project will be implemented in the West Bank and East Jerusalem, with a focus on youth residing in refugee camps, rural villages, and marginalized communities.</narrative>
  </description>
